\begin{aligned}
\overline{AC_2} &= \overline{BC_7} = 2\sqrt{2-2\cos\left(\frac{\pi}{7}\right)}, \\
\overline{AC_3} &= \overline{BC_6} = 2\sqrt{2-2\cos\left(\frac{2\pi}{7}\right)}, \\
\overline{AC_4} &= \overline{BC_5} = 2\sqrt{2-2\cos\left(\frac{3\pi}{7}\right)}. \\
\end{aligned}
\]
The product of the lengths of these twelve chords is: \[
\begin{aligned}
&\left(2\sqrt{2-2\cos\left(\frac{\pi}{7}\right)}\right)^2 \left(2\sqrt{2-2\cos\left(\frac{2\pi}{7}\right)}\right)^2 \left(2\sqrt{2-2\cos\left(\frac{3\pi}{7}\right)}\right)^2 \\
&= 2^6 \left(2-2\cos\left(\frac{\pi}{7}\right)\right)^2 \left(2-2\cos\left(\frac{2\pi}{7}\right)\right)^2 \left(2-2\cos\left(\frac{3\pi}{7}\right)\right)^2 \\
&= 64 \left(1-\cos\left(\frac{\pi}{7}\right)\right)^2 \left(1-\cos\left(\frac{2\pi}{7}\right)\right)^2 \left(1-\cos\left(\frac{3\pi}{7}\right)\right)^2.
\end{aligned}
\]
Now, use the identity $\cos(\pi - x) = -\cos(x)$ to simplify the product: \[
\begin{aligned}
\left(1-\cos\left(\frac{3\pi}{7}\right)\right)^2 &= \left(1+\cos\left(\frac{4\pi}{7}\right)\right)^2, \\
